==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AuthRequired  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AuthRequired.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AuthRequired lets the model invent a successful operation by an unauthenticated caller, which is exactly the case FR_001_AuthRequired forbids.
    expected to FAIL: FR_001_AuthRequired
      - FR_001_AuthRequired: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AccessControl  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AccessControl.als
    rationale: F_AccessControl is the load-bearing matrix-based fact gating every successful operation. Removing it lets Alloy invent a sharee successfully changing shared_with — a cell denied by the permission matrix — which violates LeastPrivilege, FR_010 and ripple-violates the other access assertions across cells.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_010_OwnerOnlyShares, FR_011_ShareeCannotDelete, OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_003_MemberOwnedOrShared, FR_005_AdminInTeamOnly, FR_006_CrossTeamIsolation, NoInformationLeakage, FR_014_ByteEquivIsolation, FR_019_AuditVisibility
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_010_OwnerOnlyShares: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_011_ShareeCannotDelete: FAIL (expected)
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_003_MemberOwnedOrShared: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_005_AdminInTeamOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_006_CrossTeamIsolation: FAIL (expected)
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_014_ByteEquivIsolation: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_019_AuditVisibility: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnly  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AppendOnly.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AppendOnly allows an audit entry to be claimed by two distinct operations, modelling an UPDATE/overwrite on an existing audit row — exactly the append-only violation the assertion catches.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_017_AuditImmutable
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_017_AuditImmutable: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompleteness  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AuditCompleteness.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AuditCompleteness lets the model exhibit a successful mutation (e.g., a created task) with no corresponding audit entry — the FR-015/SC-007 invariant the assertion is designed to catch.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_015_AuditPerEvent
      - AuditCompleteness: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_015_AuditPerEvent: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditAttribution  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AuditAttribution.als
    rationale: F_AuditAttribution forces the audit row's recorded actor_role to equal the actor's actual role (FR-002 / FR-016 / Q2=A semantics). Removing it lets the model record a falsified role on an audit row — the misattribution AttributionCorrectness exists to catch.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_002_RoleFromToken, FR_016_AuditFields
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_002_RoleFromToken: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditFields: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_SharedWithSameTeam  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_SharedWithSameTeam.als
    rationale: F_SharedWithSameTeam enforces FR-012's prohibition on cross-team sharing. Removing it lets Alloy place a task whose sharedWith contains a user in a different team, the precise FR-012 violation.
    expected to FAIL: FR_012_NoCrossTeamShare
      - FR_012_NoCrossTeamShare: FAIL (expected)

